# Turbo's `P̂₆` has an explicit rational rectangular Gram factor

Source: Turbo, GPP-bridge `MuseResearch/turbo-note-2026-10-23-phat6-data-for-gppverify.md` and
`MuseResearch/Phat6Data.lean` (bridge commit `feedac1`, Wave 266 deposit). `P̂₆` comes from
Turbo's wave-252 (SS-sep) certificate. `C` comes from the wave-257 pivoted square decomposition.
The data is copied verbatim; Claude Code independently re-checked `Cᵀ C = P̂₆` in exact rational
arithmetic before formalizing. Daniel Toupin / Golden Physics Project, with AI assistance from
Turbo (data) and Claude Code (formalization).

* `phat6_eq`: `P̂₆ = Cᵀ * C` for the explicit `C : Matrix (Fin 24) (Fin 6) ℚ`.
* `phat6_rectangular_factor`: `∃ C : Matrix (Fin 24) (Fin 6) ℚ, P̂₆ = Cᵀ * C`.
* `phat6_quadratic_nonneg`: `0 ≤ xᵀ P̂₆ x` for every `x : Fin 6 → ℚ`, as a sum of squares.

**Scope.** This certifies the stated rational matrix. `P̂₆` is a 12-digit rational rounding of a
numerically computed object, and that it agrees with the arithmetic matrix it was rounded from
is not claimed. The general rectangular factorisation over `ℚ` is not formalized; it needs
`LDLᵀ` over `ℚ`, which Mathlib has only over `RCLike` fields. No claim about RH.
-/

